# Files that must not reach the deployment.
#
# supplier-pages/ is the reason this file exists. It is 179MB — 74 saved
# supplier product pages at ~1MB of HTML each, plus 107MB of the images that
# came with them — and it was committed on 9 August. The working tree is 288MB
# total, so this one directory is 62% of everything Vercel is asked to take.
# The live site has been stuck on a build from around 6 August ever since.
#
# It is a genuinely useful thing to have: an offline copy of every supplier page
# the catalogue is audited against, which matters because D.I. Designs sits
# behind a CAPTCHA and cannot be re-fetched on demand. But it is a development
# reference. Nothing at runtime reads it, nothing imports it, and no page renders
# it — so it has no business being uploaded, built, or deployed.
#
# Note this does not shrink the git history, which is permanently 166MB heavier
# and slows every clone including the one Vercel does. Worth fixing separately.
supplier-pages/

# Sanity exports written before a destructive script runs. Restore material,
# never served.
backups/

# Written for people, not for the runtime.
docs/

# Playwright specs. They run in CI, not in production.
e2e/
